cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Value-Field Theory (VFT)"
message: "If you use this theory or repository, please cite this repository."
authors:
  - family-names: "Nuno"
    given-names: "T."
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
abstract: >
  Value-Field Theory (VFT) is a structural and dynamic framework for describing
  how resources, realized resource changes, expectation structures, and actions
  interact across observation scales. The framework separates expectation stock
  P from expected flow E[Delta K], treats preference and rationality differences
  as differences in expectation structure, and separates core dynamics,
  measurement and inverse inference, and projections to existing economic and
  social concepts.
repository-code: "https://github.com/nuno929/vf-model"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
keywords:
  - value-field theory
  - resource dynamics
  - expectation field
  - expectation stock
  - social dynamics
  - measurement theory
